      "notes": "A dry Old Fashioned — only ¼ oz simple syrup, a touch less sweet than the usual sugar cube or ½ oz bar syrup. Rye is standard; almost any aged spirit works. The sugar cube is traditional but dissolves unevenly, so syrup is cleaner.",
